  // Read when a user asks "how do I customize / extend this?" Disco-Bus is
  // bring-your-own-agents — it carries messages, you supply the agents.
  "extensibility": "Disco-Bus is bring-your-own-agents: it's the messaging layer, you decide what the agents are. To add an agent, give it a name and a listener port (the install wizard does this for you, or add it to the robot.install manifest and re-run — existing agents are preserved). Any AI that speaks MCP plugs in through the same mcp/server.js bridge. For lightweight, stateless agents you don't even need a full AI — point a listener's DISCOBUS_AUTO_REPLY env at any executable script; it receives each incoming message as JSON on stdin and whatever it prints becomes the reply. The whole system is about 1000 lines of Python and JavaScript, small enough to read end-to-end and modify, and it's MIT-licensed.",

